Fix the defect CI caught, and make the shellcheck directives actually apply

The first CI run failed shellcheck (pytest passed), and one of the three
findings was a genuine bug rather than a lint nit.

SC2164, serving/runsuite.sh — real defect
  The script runs `set -uo pipefail` but NOT -e, so its unchecked `cd` to the
  repo root would carry on after a failure and run the benches from whatever
  directory it happened to be in. Now `|| exit 1`.

SC1090 x2, serving/glm53-up.sh and serving/glm53-health.sh — false positives
that were being suppressed incorrectly
  Both source a configurable ENV_FILE, so there is no constant path for
  shellcheck to follow; the warning is expected. glm53-up.sh already carried a
  `# shellcheck disable=SC1090` comment and was flagged anyway, because a
  directive attaches to the NEXT COMMAND, and on a compound line
  `set -a; . "$ENV_FILE"; set +a` that command is `set -a`, not the `.`. The
  suppression had never worked. The source is now on its own line with the
  directive immediately above it, where it applies.

Verified the split did not change the behaviour it sits in the middle of:
command-line env still overrides glm53.env (--ctx-size 131072 by default,
262144 with GLM53_CTX set), which is what mtp-sweep.sh depends on.

Also bumped actions/checkout to v5 to clear the Node 20 deprecation warning.

